---A clickable UI element. Text and Image can each be empty; both filled shows an icon and a label. Fires Activated when clicked. The old name TextButton still loads.
---@class TextButton: Instance
---@field Class string Space-separated CSS class names used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Id string The CSS identifier used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Position UDim2 The top-left position relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field Size UDim2 The size relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field BackgroundColor3 Color3 The button's background color.
---@field BackgroundTransparency number The background opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Text string The text to display.
---@field TextColor3 Color3 The text color.
---@field TextSize number The text size in pixels.
---@field Image string The project-relative path of an icon. Empty shows no picture. With Text, the icon sits beside the label.
---@field ImageTransparency number The icon opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Visible boolean If false, this button is hidden and cannot be activated.
---@field Activated Signal Fires when the player clicks or taps this button. The handler gets no arguments; LocalScripts only.

---A UI element that displays an image from the project. It is not clickable.
---@class ImageLabel: Instance
---@field Class string Space-separated CSS class names used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Id string The CSS identifier used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Position UDim2 The top-left position relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field Size UDim2 The size relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field BackgroundColor3 Color3 The image label's background color.
---@field BackgroundTransparency number The background opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Image string The project-relative path of the image to display.
---@field ImageTransparency number The image opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Visible boolean If false, this image is hidden.

---A box the player can type in. MultiLine off (the default): Enter finishes. MultiLine on: Enter is a new line and clicking away finishes. Fires FocusLost.
---@class TextBox: Instance
---@field Class string Space-separated CSS class names used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Id string The CSS identifier used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Position UDim2 The top-left position relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field Size UDim2 The size relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field BackgroundColor3 Color3 The box's background color.
---@field BackgroundTransparency number The background opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Text string The text the player has typed.
---@field Placeholder string Grey text shown while Text is empty.
---@field TextColor3 Color3 The text color.
---@field TextSize number The text size in pixels.
---@field MultiLine boolean If false, Enter finishes typing. If true, Enter starts a new line and clicking away finishes typing.
---@field Visible boolean If false, this text box is hidden.
---@field FocusLost Signal Fires when the player finishes typing: Enter on a one-line box, or clicking away (or Escape) on any box. The handler gets no arguments; LocalScripts only.

---Shows one child Frame at a time, chosen by CurrentPage (the Frame's Name). Other children, such as a title, stay visible.
---@class PageLayout: Instance
---@field Class string Space-separated CSS class names used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Id string The CSS identifier used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Position UDim2 The top-left position relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field Size UDim2 The size relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field BackgroundColor3 Color3 The layout's background color.
---@field BackgroundTransparency number The background opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Visible boolean If false, this layout and its pages are hidden.
---@field CurrentPage string The Name of the child Frame to show. Empty shows the first child Frame. A name that matches no Frame is rejected and the current page stays.

---Lays its children out as equal cells, left to right then top to bottom. Columns is how many cells share a row.
---@class Table: Instance
---@field Class string Space-separated CSS class names used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Id string The CSS identifier used to style this UI Instance.
---@field Position UDim2 The top-left position relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field Size UDim2 The size relative to the parent, in scale and pixel offsets.
---@field BackgroundColor3 Color3 The table's background color.
---@field BackgroundTransparency number The background opacity: 0 is opaque and 1 is transparent.
---@field Visible boolean If false, this table is hidden.
---@field Columns number How many cells sit in one row. Cells are the table's children, left to right then top to bottom, each the same size.

---UI that floats in the world, parented to a Part or MeshPart and drawn on the screen UI overlay. Size is on-screen; StudsOffset moves it in world studs.
---@class BillboardGui: Instance
---@field Class string Space-separated CSS class names used to style descendants of this billboard.
---@field Id string The CSS identifier used to style this billboard.
---@field Enabled boolean If false, this billboard is not drawn.
---@field Size UDim2 The on-screen size, in scale of the viewport plus a pixel offset.
---@field StudsOffset Vector3 World studs added to the parent part's position. The offset is not rotated with the part.
---@field MaxDistance number The billboard hides past this many studs from the camera. 0 shows it at any distance.

---A sound effect or music track that scripts can play. Spatial sounds sit on a part and get quieter with distance from the camera.
---@class Sound: Instance
---@field SoundId string The audio file inside the project folder, such as "assets/audio/chime.wav".
---@field Volume number Playback volume as a non-negative amplitude; 1 is the original level and 0 is silent.
---@field Looped boolean If true, playback repeats until Stop is called or the game session stops.
---@field PlaybackSpeed number How fast the sound plays: 1 is normal, 2 twice as fast (and an octave higher), 0.5 half. Changes apply while it plays.
---@field Playing boolean True while the sound plays. Set it to false to pause and true to carry on. Saved as true, the sound plays as soon as the game starts, with no script needed.
---@field Spatial boolean If true, the sound is placed in the world and panned as the camera moves. If false, it plays the same in both ears.
---@field Position Vector3 Where a spatial sound plays from, in studs, when it is not inside a Part, MeshPart or Terrain. Inside one of those, that ancestor's Position is used instead.
---@field RollOffMinDistance number A spatial sound stays at full volume within this many studs of the camera. 10 by default. Not used while Spatial is false.
---@field RollOffMaxDistance number A spatial sound is silent from this many studs out. 150 by default. Kept at least as large as RollOffMinDistance.
---@field Ended Signal Fires when the sound plays to its end. Looped sounds, and sounds stopped with Stop, don't fire it.
local SoundClass = {}

---Plays this sound from the start, with its SoundId, Volume, PlaybackSpeed, Looped and Spatial, and sets Playing to true. Playing it again restarts it; stopping the game session stops all sounds.
---@return nil
function SoundClass:Play() end

---Stops this sound and sets Playing to false. The next Play starts from the beginning.
---@return nil
function SoundClass:Stop() end

---Pauses this sound where it is (sets Playing to false). Resume carries on from there.
---@return nil
function SoundClass:Pause() end

---Carries on playing a paused sound, or plays a stopped one from the start (sets Playing to true).
---@return nil
function SoundClass:Resume() end


---A light that shines in all directions from just above its parent part. Inserting one with no part selected also inserts an anchored lamp.
---@class PointLight: Instance
---@field Enabled boolean If false, the light is off.
---@field Color Color3 The light's color.
---@field Brightness number How bright the light is.
---@field Range number How far the light reaches, in studs.

---A light that shines in a cone from just above its parent part. Inserting one with no part selected also inserts an anchored lamp.
---@class SpotLight: Instance
---@field Enabled boolean If false, the light is off.
---@field Color Color3 The light's color.
---@field Brightness number How bright the light is.
---@field Range number How far the light reaches, in studs.
---@field Angle number The full width of the cone, in degrees.
---@field Direction Vector3 The way the beam points, relative to the parent part.

---Gives off particles (sparks, smoke, fire, stars...) from inside its parent part, shown in the editor and the game.
---@class ParticleEmitter: Instance
---@field Enabled boolean If false, it stops giving off particles; those already out live on.
---@field ParticleType EnumItem.ParticleType|"Circle"|"Spark"|"Smoke"|"Fire"|"Star"|"Magic" The built-in picture each particle shows: Circle, Spark, Smoke, Fire, Star or Magic. Texture, if set, is used instead.
---@field Texture string An image file inside the project folder each particle shows instead of ParticleType, such as "assets/particles/spark_01.png" (Kenney's free Particle Pack works well). Its alpha is the shape; it's tinted by Color.
---@field Rate number How many particles a second it gives off while Enabled.
---@field Lifetime number How many seconds each particle lives (each one a little more or less).
---@field Speed number How fast particles leave, in studs a second, along Direction.
---@field Direction Vector3 The way particles leave, relative to the parent part (up by default).
---@field SpreadAngle number How wide the cone particles leave in is, in degrees: 0 is a straight line, 360 every way.
---@field Acceleration Vector3 Added to every particle's speed each second, in world studs (gravity is Vector3.new(0, -196.2, 0)).
---@field Drag number How quickly particles slow down: 0 never, higher sooner.
---@field WindAffectsDrag boolean If true, Drag slows particles toward workspace.GlobalWind instead of to a stop, so the wind carries them. Needs a Drag above 0.
---@field Size number How many studs across a particle is when it's born.
---@field SizeEnd number How many studs across a particle is when it dies; it grows or shrinks smoothly.
---@field Color Color3 A particle's color when it's born. It tints the picture.
---@field ColorEnd Color3 A particle's color when it dies; it fades smoothly from Color.
---@field Transparency number From 0 (solid) to 1 (invisible) when a particle is born.
---@field TransparencyEnd number From 0 (solid) to 1 (invisible) when a particle dies.
---@field Rotation number How far each particle is turned when it's born, in degrees.
---@field RotSpeed number How fast particles spin, in degrees a second.
---@field LightEmission number From 0 (particles paint over what's behind them, like smoke) to 1 (they add their light, like fire and sparks).
---@field Brightness number How brightly particles glow: 1 is their color as it is; higher values bloom.
local ParticleEmitterClass = {}

---Gives off this many particles at once (up to 1000), even while Enabled is false, such as a burst of sparks when something breaks.
---@param count number
---@return nil
function ParticleEmitterClass:Emit(count) end


---Inside a Part, MeshPart, Model, ScreenGui or UI element: plays animation on its parent while the game runs: its state machine, if it has one, and the AnimationTracks loaded with LoadAnimation.
---@class Animator: Instance
---@field StateMachine string The state machine file it plays on its parent, inside the project folder, such as "assets/animations/hero/hero.statemachine.json". Empty plays only the AnimationTracks loaded on it. The Animator tab makes and edits them.
---@field Enabled boolean If false, everything it animates holds still: the animator stops moving on.
---@field Speed number Plays everything this many times as fast (1 is normal, 0 pauses).
---@field CurrentState string The name of the state playing (read-only; use `Play` to change it). Empty until the animator first runs.
---@field StateChanged Signal Fires when the animator moves to another state. The handler gets the new state's name, then the old one's: `function(state, previous) ... end`.
---@field AnimationEvent Signal Fires when a playing clip passes one of its animation events. The handler gets the event's name.
local AnimatorClass = {}

---Sets a Bool parameter, such as `IsGrounded`: something that stays true or false until it's changed.
---@param name string
---@param value boolean
---@return nil
function AnimatorClass:SetBool(name, value) end

---A Bool parameter's value.
---@param name string
---@return boolean
function AnimatorClass:GetBool(name) end

---Sets a Number parameter, such as `Speed`: a value that changes gradually, for conditions and blend trees.
---@param name string
---@param value number
---@return nil
function AnimatorClass:SetNumber(name, value) end

---A Number parameter's value.
---@param name string
---@return number
function AnimatorClass:GetNumber(name) end

---Sets a Trigger parameter, such as `Jump`: a one-time request, used up by the transition it starts.
---@param name string
---@return nil
function AnimatorClass:SetTrigger(name) end

---Clears a Trigger that no transition has used yet.
---@param name string
---@return nil
function AnimatorClass:ResetTrigger(name) end

---Switches to the state named `state`, from its start, blending from the pose now over `blend` seconds (0.25 if left out; 0 snaps).
---@param state string
---@param blend? number
---@return nil
function AnimatorClass:Play(state, blend) end

---Loads `animation` (an Animation, whose Clip names the clip) on this Animator and returns an AnimationTrack to play, stop and blend over the state machine.
---@param animation Animation
---@return AnimationTrack
function AnimatorClass:LoadAnimation(animation) end

---The AnimationTracks loaded on this Animator that are playing now.
---@return AnimationTrack[]
function AnimatorClass:GetPlayingAnimationTracks() end


---Points at a clip (`*.anim.json`). Load it with `animator:LoadAnimation(animation)` to play it, or tick AutoPlay to play it when the game starts.
---@class Animation: Instance
---@field Clip string The clip file inside the project folder, such as "assets/animations/Door/Open.anim.json".
---@field AutoPlay boolean If true, the Animator on the same parent plays it by itself when the game starts.
---@field Enabled boolean If false, playback pauses at its current time; set true to continue.
---@field Speed number Plays the clip this many times as fast (1 is normal, 0 pauses).
---@field Looped boolean If true, playback repeats instead of firing Completed at the end.
---@field Completed Signal Fires when `animation:Play()` reaches the end of a clip that doesn't loop. The handler gets no arguments.
---@field AnimationEvent Signal Fires when `animation:Play()` passes one of the clip's events. The handler gets the event's name.
local AnimationClass = {}

---Plays this Animation's clip from the start, through the Animator on the same parent. `animator:LoadAnimation(animation)` is the newer way, with fades and weights.
---@return nil
function AnimationClass:Play() end

---Stops playback and goes back to the start of the clip.
---@return nil
function AnimationClass:Stop() end

---Pauses at the current time. Resume continues from there.
---@return nil
function AnimationClass:Pause() end

---Continues after Pause.
---@return nil
function AnimationClass:Resume() end


---One Animation loaded on an Animator, from `animator:LoadAnimation(animation)`: play, stop and blend it over the state machine.
---@class AnimationTrack: Instance
---@field IsPlaying boolean True from Play until Stop, or until a clip that doesn't loop ends (read-only).
---@field Length number The clip's length in seconds (read-only; 0 until the clip has been read, a frame after LoadAnimation).
---@field Looped boolean Whether it plays again from the start when it ends. Starts as the clip's own.
---@field Speed number How fast it plays (read-only; use AdjustSpeed).
---@field TimePosition number Seconds into the clip. Set it to jump there.
---@field WeightCurrent number How much it counts now, from 0 to 1, while fading (read-only).
---@field WeightTarget number The weight it's fading to (read-only; use AdjustWeight).
---@field Animation Animation The Animation it was loaded from (read-only).
---@field Stopped Signal Fires when the track has stopped: after Stop's fade, or at the end of a clip that doesn't loop.
---@field KeyframeReached Signal Fires each time the track passes one of the clip's events. The handler gets the event's name; GetMarkerReachedSignal hears one name.
local AnimationTrackClass = {}

---Plays the clip from its start, fading in over `fadeTime` seconds (0.1 if left out) to `weight` (1), at `speed` (1). Where it and what plays under it animate the same thing, the track started last wins.
---@param fadeTime? number
---@param weight? number
---@param speed? number
---@return nil
function AnimationTrackClass:Play(fadeTime, weight, speed) end

---Stops it, fading out over `fadeTime` seconds (0.1 if left out). Stopped fires once it has faded out.
---@param fadeTime? number
---@return nil
function AnimationTrackClass:Stop(fadeTime) end

---Plays it this many times as fast from now (1 is normal, 0 holds, negative plays backwards).
---@param speed? number
---@return nil
function AnimationTrackClass:AdjustSpeed(speed) end

---Fades how much it counts to `weight` (0 to 1) over `fadeTime` seconds (0.1 if left out).
---@param weight? number
---@param fadeTime? number
---@return nil
function AnimationTrackClass:AdjustWeight(weight, fadeTime) end

---An event that fires each time the track passes the clip's event named `name`. The handler gets the name.
---@param name string
---@return Signal
function AnimationTrackClass:GetMarkerReachedSignal(name) end


---A landscape: a heightfield shaped in the editor's Terrain Studio, drawn with its TerrainLayers and colliding as its ground. Position is the middle of its footprint at the bottom of its height range; Size is its width, height range and length.
---@class Terrain: Instance
---@field Position Vector3 The middle of the terrain's bottom: its lowest possible ground.
---@field Size Vector3 Width (X), height range (Y) and length (Z) in studs. Heights are stored as parts of the height range, so changing Y stretches the hills.
---@field CastShadow boolean Whether the terrain casts shadows.
---@field CanCollide boolean Whether parts and characters stand on the terrain.
---@field DataFolder string The project folder its heights and painted materials are saved in, such as "assets/terrain/Terrain". The editor picks it.

---Inside a Terrain: one material it's painted with (a tint, texture maps and tiling), and an optional rule that lays it down by height and slope.
---@class TerrainLayer: Instance
---@field Color Color3 Tints the layer's color map, or is its color without one.
---@field ColorMap string The layer's color texture, relative to the project folder. Empty means none.
---@field NormalMap string The layer's normal map. Empty means none.
---@field RoughnessMap string The layer's roughness map. Empty means none.
---@field MetalnessMap string The layer's metalness map. Empty means none.
---@field AmbientOcclusionMap string The layer's ambient occlusion map. Empty means none.
---@field HeightMap string The layer's height map: light is high. Where layers meet, the higher one shows through.
---@field Metalness number 0 to 1: how metallic the layer is, without a metalness map.
---@field Roughness number 0 to 1: how rough the layer is, without a roughness map.
---@field NormalStrength number Scales the normal map's bumps.
---@field NormalMapDirectX boolean True for a DirectX-style normal map, whose green points down.
---@field RoughnessChannel EnumItem.TextureChannel|"Red"|"Green"|"Blue"|"Alpha" Which channel of RoughnessMap holds the roughness.
---@field InvertRoughness boolean Reads RoughnessMap as smoothness (1 minus the value).
---@field MetalnessChannel EnumItem.TextureChannel|"Red"|"Green"|"Blue"|"Alpha" Which channel of MetalnessMap holds the metalness.
---@field AmbientOcclusionChannel EnumItem.TextureChannel|"Red"|"Green"|"Blue"|"Alpha" Which channel of AmbientOcclusionMap holds the occlusion.
---@field TileSize number Studs one copy of the textures covers.
---@field TextureRotation number Turns the textures, in degrees.
---@field Triplanar boolean Projects the textures from the sides too, so cliffs don't stretch them.
---@field AntiTiling number 0 to 1: mixes in a larger, turned copy of the textures so repeats show less.
---@field HeightBlend number 0 to 1: how sharply layers meet where they have height maps.
---@field AutoEnabled boolean Whether the layer lays itself down by its height and slope rule.
---@field MinHeight number The rule's lowest height, in studs above the terrain's bottom.
---@field MaxHeight number The rule's highest height, in studs above the terrain's bottom.
---@field HeightFade number Studs over which the rule fades at its heights.
---@field MinSlope number The rule's gentlest slope, in degrees from flat.
---@field MaxSlope number The rule's steepest slope, in degrees from flat.
---@field SlopeFade number Degrees over which the rule fades at its slopes.
---@field RuleStrength number 0 to 1: how fully the layer covers where its rule holds.
---@field RuleNoise number 0 to 1: breaks the rule's edges up with noise.
---@field NoiseScale number Studs across the rule's noise patches.

